### Remaining Concerns
1. **§5 sets up a payoff §8 delivers ~1,400 words later.** "Hold this episode next to the video that came a year later" asks the reader to hold a thread across the morning-routine section, the Rabbit Hole, and the father section. The two new bridges now make that interval read as *building* toward the return rather than detouring, but the cleanest structural fix would be moving §7 (father) ahead of §6 (morning routine) so the Rabbit Hole and the morning section sit adjacent to §8. That's a reordering call, not a bridging one, so I left it to you.
2. **The title's rule goes dormant.** "Tolerant with others, strict with yourself" is named in the intro and not touched again until §8. §5 is the natural place for a half-sentence callback — the Naval Academy *is* him being strict with others — but the word ceiling gave me nothing to spend. Worth one sentence if you cut something first.
